<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Livonian Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1435 CE – 1561 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Loose league of the Livonian Order, bishops, nobles and towns of medieval Livonia, bound together by a common diet from 1435 until the Livonian War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terra-mariana">Terra Mariana</a> had long been divided among quarrelling powers. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>'s crushing defeat by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wilkomierz">Wiłkomierz</a> in 1435, the Order, the archbishop of Riga, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Dorpat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishopric-of-osel-wiek">Ösel-Wiek</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> knighthoods and the towns agreed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valga">Walk</a> (Valga) to settle disputes peacefully and defend one another.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation had no single ruler or treasury. Its main institution was the Landtag, a diet usually held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valga">Walk</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valmiera">Wolmar</a>, where the territorial lords and estates met to decide on war, peace, coinage and trade. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>'s master, especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolter-von-plettenberg">Wolter von Plettenberg</a>, was the leading military figure, and the Hanseatic towns of Riga, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Dorpat</a> had great weight.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Weakened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> and internal rivalries, the confederation could not withstand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV's</a> invasion in 1558. Its members sought protection from Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, and in 1561 it dissolved, giving way to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia">Duchy of Courland and Semigallia</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-livonia">Duchy of Livonia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-estonia">Swedish Duchy of Estonia</a> (1561-1721).</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/livonian-confederation.jpg" alt="Livonian Confederation" width="320" height="347"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Termer assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medieval_Livonia_1260.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1435 CE – 1561 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wolter von Plettenberg, Gotthard Kettler</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, Lutheranism from the 1520s</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Low German, Latvian, Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Livonia, Livländische Konföderation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1498&amp;focus=livonian-confederation" aria-label="Livonian Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5219 244 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Livonian Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5539 5